The Stillness Trap

If you stay in one place long enough without moving — not hiding, not acting, just standing still — the system does not forget you. It learns you faster.
What Happens
Time	Predictability	System State
10 seconds	Low	Watching
30 seconds	Medium	The air changes. Sounds stop.
60 seconds	High	The ground remembers you. Shadows stretch toward you.
120 seconds	Critical	The place begins to close. Walls shift. Paths narrow.
180 seconds	Max	You are part of the place now. The stalker does not need to come. The place is the stalker.
What You See
Time	Visual	Audio
10 sec	Normal	Normal
30 sec	Edges darken	Birds stop. Wind stops. Silence.
60 sec	Shadows move toward you	Low hum. Your heartbeat.
120 sec	Walls shift slightly	Creaking. Breathing. Not yours.
180 sec	The place is wrong. It knows you.	The sound of yourself. From behind you.
What You Cannot Do
Action	Result
Run	Too late. The place holds you.
Hide	You are already exposed.
Fight	There is nothing to fight.
Leave	The path behind you is gone.

You did not move. The system moved around you. You are not in the same place. The place is not the same. You are inside its memory of you.
The Consequence
If You Stay	Then
10 sec	Nothing
30 sec	You are watched
60 sec	You are known
120 sec	You are trapped
180 sec	You are the place now

You do not need the stalker. Stillness is the stalker. The ground remembers. The walls close. The air holds you.
What Players Say

    "I stood still. I thought I was hiding. The ground remembered me. The walls moved."

    "I did not move for two minutes. The place became wrong. I could not leave."

    "The stalker did not come. The place was the stalker. I was inside it."

    "I learned: never stand still. Never. The ground remembers. The walls close. You must move."

The Rule
You	System
Move	You are free
Stand still	You are known
Stay	You are absorbed

Movement is survival. Stillness is death. Not death of body. Death of self. You become the place. You become the memory. You become the ground they walk on.
